cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Cite the artifact you used and the block it was pinned at, not the repository
  as a whole. A figure here is only meaningful with its pinned block, and most
  artifacts carry their own expiry. The four identifiers worth citing are
  declared in STABLE-LINKS.json; the licence split is declared in
  LICENSE-MAP.json.
title: >-
  Executability report: reproducible exit-depth measurement, published with the
  instrument's own failures
abstract: >-
  Independent measurement of what a position can actually be sold for on
  permissionless venues, at a pinned block, from public contract state only.
  Reads are pinned by block hash with requireCanonical and archived with
  digests; generated documents byte-reproduce from their generators; claims are
  compiled into criteria that run in CI with three exit codes, so that "we did
  not look" is never reported as "we looked and it was fine", and each
  criterion states what it does not establish. The instrument's own failures
  are published as a numbered archive, each entry recording which side of
  publication it landed on and what it corrupted.
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: dirkdiggler1026
    website: "https://dirkdiggler1026.github.io/executability-report/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/dirkdiggler1026/executability-report"
